{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Peace be to you, etc.</b> The man said this on his own initiative, without knowing what Joseph's intention was. And according to the words of the Sages, whose memory is for a blessing (Tanchuma), who said that he was Menasseh — the son's insight surpassed the father's, and he knew that he would agree to his words. And his saying <b>do not be afraid</b> is because the fear was recognized in their faces, for they were afraid, as it is written (Genesis 43:18): ״וַיִּירְאוּ הָאֲנָשִׁים״." "<b>He has given you treasure.</b> Meaning: some man buried the silver there, and HaShem gave it to you by way of the owners' despair [of recovering it], and the children of Noah are not commanded to announce a lost object. And to strengthen their heart he brought Simeon out to them, to show that all was well with them."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:21.935503865Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}